WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.900
If you are new to Cloud Code, do not watch another tutorial

00:02.900 --> 00:04.800
until you do this one thing first.

00:04.800 --> 00:07.320
And Droppic has released a GitHub repository

00:07.320 --> 00:09.640
and they are the company behind Cloud Code.

00:09.640 --> 00:12.000
This repository includes skills, cookbooks,

00:12.000 --> 00:13.880
prompt engineering guides, full courses,

00:13.880 --> 00:16.360
quick start resources, and even the source code

00:16.360 --> 00:18.160
for Cloud Code itself.

00:18.160 --> 00:20.560
Many people spend time scrolling through content,

00:20.560 --> 00:23.280
installing random skills, and becoming overwhelmed.

00:23.280 --> 00:25.960
A more effective approach is to use this repository

00:25.960 --> 00:26.960
as a foundation.

00:26.960 --> 00:28.720
You can bring it into Cloud Code and use it

00:28.720 --> 00:31.240
to explore the basics, learn structured workflows,

00:31.240 --> 00:32.880
and build a strong starting point.

00:32.880 --> 00:34.960
This allows you to work from a reliable source,

00:34.960 --> 00:37.280
rather than relying on trial and error.

00:37.280 --> 00:40.160
If anyone understands how to use Cloud Code effectively,

00:40.160 --> 00:41.720
it is the team that created it.

00:41.720 --> 00:43.280
You can find the repository link

00:43.280 --> 00:45.360
and a starter workflow in the caption.

00:45.360 --> 00:47.520
DM's send, and I'll send you the link.

